  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, thanks for letting us know. I checked your laptop (BL-LT-0101) and it actually looks healthy right now: about 310 GB of its 512 GB is free (around 60%), and it isn't reporting any storage warnings. So I'm not sure the warning came from that main drive. To figure out where it's coming from, could you tell me: 1) Is the warning on your Brightline laptop BL-LT-0101, or on another computer? 2) What exactly does the message say, and which drive letter does it mention (for example C: or D:)? A screenshot would be great. 3) Do you have a USB drive, external disk or SD card plugged in? 4) Roughly when did you last see it? If it turns out a drive really is filling up, here are some safe things you can do: empty the Recycle Bin and clear out your Downloads folder, go to Settings > System > Storage > Temporary files and remove temporary files, and turn on OneDrive Files On-Demand so synced files stay in the cloud until you open them. Once I hear back, I'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "User is a VIP (CEO) and reported a low disk space warning. Her account is active and the only assigned device is BL-LT-0101. check_device_status for BL-LT-0101: online, last check-in 2026-10-09 14:22 UTC, 512 GB total, 310 GB free (60.5%), no warnings. This is well above the 10% threshold in KB-017, so the device data doesn't back up the report. Possible causes: an external or secondary drive, a different or personal device, a one-off temporary spike, or a misread message. I asked the user for the device, the exact message and drive letter, a screenshot, and whether any removable media is plugged in. I gave her the self-service cleanup steps from KB-017. I have no remote cleanup tool, so no action was taken. If she confirms a real shortage on the C: drive, re-check the device and escalate per KB-017 if free space stays under 10% after cleanup.",
